    "scientific_verdict": "Across k in {2, 3} oracle calls and prime/prime-power moduli, the secret-variance Var_s[P_{epsilon, sigma}(x | s)] equals the exact Parseval sum of squared moduli of the non-zero difference-fiber harmonics C_{epsilon, sigma}(delta; x) (delta != 0). Every harmonic obeys Hermitian conjugate symmetry C(-delta; x) = conj(C(delta; x)) and sums to zero across outcomes x in {0, ..., D-1} for all delta != 0, while destructive bilinear Fourier phase interference suppresses total L2 signal energy strictly below the 4-tuple Kronecker multiplicity bound (1/D^{2k+1}) sum_{delta != 0} M_epsilon(delta)^2."
  },
  "theorems": [
    {
      "id": "T1",
      "name": "Exact 4-Tuple Kronecker Difference-Variety Parseval Identity",
      "statement": "For any k-call schedule (epsilon, sigma) and readout outcome x in {0, ..., D-1}, the secret-Fourier harmonics C_(epsilon, sigma)(delta; x) = sum_(Delta tau_epsilon(w, w') = delta) B_(epsilon, sigma)(w, w'; x) satisfy E_s[P(x | s)] = C(0; x) and Var_(s ~ Z_q^n)[P_(epsilon, sigma)(x | s)] = sum_(delta != 0) |C_(epsilon, sigma)(delta; x)|^2."
    },
    {
      "id": "T2",
      "name": "Hermitian Conjugate Symmetry and Outcome Sum Annihilation of Non-Zero Harmonics",
      "statement": "For every difference vector delta in Z_q^n and outcome x, C_(epsilon, sigma)(-delta mod q; x) = conj(C_(epsilon, sigma)(delta; x)), and for every non-zero delta != 0, sum_(x=0)^(D-1) C_(epsilon, sigma)(delta; x) = 0 identically."
    },
    {
      "id": "T3",
      "name": "4-Tuple Kronecker Multiplicity Bound on Total L2 Secret Signal Energy",
      "statement": "With M_epsilon(delta) = |{(w, w') : Delta tau_epsilon(w, w') = delta}|, sum_delta M_epsilon(delta) = D^(2k), M_epsilon(0) = |V_epsilon(f)|, and total L2 secret signal energy E_(epsilon, sigma) = sum_x Var_s[P(x | s)] <= (1 / D^(2k+1)) * sum_(delta != 0) M_epsilon(delta)^2."
    }
  ],
  "title": "Native Higher-Call Kronecker Moment-Rank Bridge: 4-Tuple Difference-Variety Parseval Identity, Harmonic Conjugate Symmetry, and L2 Signal Energy Bounds"
